@startuml component
title proc_macro_flow — crate structure

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "proc_macro_flow\n(facade)" as facade {
  [lib.rs] as Facade
  note right of Facade
    pub use of both crates.
    Re-exports only MACROS from the
    derive crate — see the constraint below.

    Also HOSTS THE DERIVE PROOF, because
    it is the nearest crate that can.
  end note
}

package "proc_macro_flow_traits\n(ordinary lib)" as traits {
  [extractor] as T_Extractor
  [resolution] as T_Resolution
  [meta] as T_Meta
  [vocab] as T_Vocab
  [visitable] as T_Visitable
  [processor] as T_Processor
  [generator] as T_Generator
  [render] as T_Render
  [node] as T_Node

  note right of T_Vocab
    names! vocabulary! flag!
    name_value! leaf! meta_list!
    variants! + walk
    see 08-class-vocab
  end note

  note bottom of T_Processor
    Processor + process_each / process_maybe
    optional stage; identity is derived
  end note
  note bottom of T_Generator
    Generator + emit / emit_errors
    stub ALWAYS goes out beside the errors
  end note
  note bottom of T_Render
    Diagnose + render + combined
    one walk, every reason in the tree
    see 03-pipeline-status
  end note

  note left of T_Meta
    ""pub use syn"" lives here too, so
    generated code can name ""syn::Error""
    without the AUTHOR'S crate depending
    on syn under that exact name.
    (#traits/reexport-syn)
  end note
}

package "proc_macro_flow_derive\n(proc-macro = true)" as derive {
  package "derive/" as derive_mod {
    [derive_extractor] as D_DE
    [derive_validate] as D_DV
    [derive_processor] as D_DP
    [derive_syntax] as D_DS
    [ext: extension traits] as D_EXT
  }
  package "base/extractor" as base_extractor {
    [StructExtraction] as D_Struct
    [FieldExtraction] as D_Field
  }
  package "base/syntax" as base_syntax {
    [SyntaxFieldAttributeExtraction] as D_Syntax
    [worked_rs_tests] as D_Worked
  }
}

cloud "external" {
  [heck] as Heck
  [syn 3] as Syn
  [quote] as Quote
  [proc-macro2] as PM2
}

derive ..> traits : depends
facade ..> traits
facade ..> derive
traits ..> Syn
traits ..> Quote
traits ..> PM2
derive ..> Syn
derive ..> Heck : case conversion at\nEXPANSION time only

note as Constraint
  **Why two crates**

  VERIFIED: rustc rejects a `pub` non-macro
  item in a proc-macro crate outright —
  "proc-macro crate types cannot export any
  items other than functions tagged with
  ""#[proc_macro*]"".

  So every type that must be NAMEABLE from
  outside lives in proc_macro_flow_traits.
  The derive crate keeps only the macro
  entry points and its own stage impls.

  (#syntax/placement, #pipeline/relocate-traits)
end note

Constraint .. derive

note as CannotSelfHost
  **A derive crate cannot use its own derives.**

  VERIFIED, quoting rustc:
  ""can't use a procedural macro from the same crate that defines it""
  So
  StructExtraction and FieldExtraction — which
  sit in ""base/extractor"" — can NEVER carry
  ""#[derive(Extractor)]"" where they live.

  They stay hand-written as the bootstrap, and
  the FACADE hosts the proof instead: it depends
  on both crates, so it declares the equivalent
  extraction with the derives and asserts the
  generated tree matches.

  That is also the facade's only real job.
  (#derive/cannot-self-host, #facade/hosts-the-proof)
end note

CannotSelfHost .. derive_mod

note as TraitHome
  **#pipeline/relocate-traits is CLOSED.**

  Extractor, Validate and Visitable have moved
  into the traits crate. The urgency had lapsed
  when grammar types stopped implementing them,
  then came back for a different reason:
  ""#[derive(Extractor)]"" on a USER's type means
  the trait has to be nameable from outside.

  ""Sourced"" did not move — it was DELETED. The
  source rides on ""Extracted"", so a trait asking
  every extractor to store and return the same
  node was a second answer to one question.
end note

TraitHome .. traits

@enduml
